  "id": "Compound::DB00590 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Doxazosin exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c19, which is a key enzyme involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of Cyp2c19 in the arachidonic acid epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities, both of which are critical for the production of bioactive lipid mediators. These activities are ultimately linked to the participation of Cyp2d6, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Doxazosin influences the expression or activity of Cyp2d6. The shared involvement of Cyp2c19 in multiple metabolic pathways indicates a plausible, biologically relevant interaction between Doxazosin and Cyp2d6. The evidence is supported by consistent scores across different paths, suggesting a robust and well-defined mechanistic link. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2c19 as a central mediator in the metabolic effects of Doxazosin on Cyp2d6.",
